.TH DYNAMIC_QUEUE_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
dynamic_queue_create \- create a dynamic (unbounded) queue
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

dynamic_queue_create(err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates an unbounded queue implemented as a linked list. Send operations
never block (queue can grow indefinitely). Uses standard malloc/free.

This is a convenience macro for dynamic_queue_create_with_mprocs() with
NULL memory management procedures.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
err_str  Optional pointer to receive error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to newly created dynamic queue on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
All operations on this queue are thread-safe
Queue must be destroyed with dynamic_queue_destroy() when done
fork(2) is safe with respect to this queue's own internal locking: a
lock held by some other thread at the instant of the fork is never
inherited by the child already locked. The queue owns no thread of
its own, so one already live and in active use across the fork
remains fully usable on both sides afterward.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR dynamic_queue_create_with_mprocs (3),
.BR dynamic_queue_destroy (3)
